the corresponding symbols are different. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Сhris thinks that each three strings with different indices constitute a single triple. Chris's delusion is that he will wake up only if he counts the number of such string triples "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" that the sum "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"H(a, b) + H(b, c) + H(c, a)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is maximal among all the string triples constructed from the dreamed strings."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Chris wake up from this nightmare!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains two space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ m ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the length and the number of strings. The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the description of the strings. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line contains two space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"fi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ si ≤ 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ fi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the description of the string with index "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"; that means that the first "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"fi"},{"kind":"text","text":" bits of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th string are equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the remaining "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - fi"},{"kind":"text","text":" bits are equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 - si"},{"kind":"text","text":". There can be multiple equal strings in Chris's dream."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer, the number of such string triples among the given that the sum of the Hamming distances between the strings of the triple is maximal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 4\n0 3\n0 5\n1 4\n1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 4\n1 5\n0 5\n0 5\n1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"406E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/406/problem/E"}